// <auto-generated> Tools/PakReader `walls` - do not edit by hand.
//
// Every placed actor on the Athena map whose CLASS is a building wall - 10329 of them, swept from all
// 455 Athena .umap packages. A door is one of these; so is a plain wall.
//
// WHAT THIS GATE IS FOR. An interaction arrives as a client-supplied actor PATH, and acting on it
// means building an ABuildingWall stand-in and pushing WALL HANDLES at it. If the actor's real class
// is not a wall, that is a handle the class does not have, and the client DROPS THE CONNECTION -
// which is exactly what `Prop_Athena_Doorbell_Interactable_2` did (its class is
// `BuildingPropSimpleInteract`). So the question this table answers is "is it safe to send wall
// properties to this actor", and nothing else.
//
// IT DOES NOT ASK WHETHER THE ACTOR HAS A DOOR. An earlier version did, by requiring "Door" in the
// class name, and that excluded `Rural_House_Wall_9_C` - a `Parent_BuildingWall_C` subclass with a
// door in it - so that door could never be opened. Whether a wall has a door is the client's
// business: it owns the mesh and the prompt, and OnRep_bDoorOpen on a wall without one does nothing.
// Re-adding a name filter here would re-break it.
//
// The gate that works is the class ASSET's location - only walls live under
// Building/ActorBlueprints/.../Wall/ - which is checkable offline and nowhere else. An actor's NAME
// predicts nothing: `BP_TRV_CAS_TudorArch_Castle_Wall_423` is a door and `Prop_Athena_Doorbell_
// Interactable_2` is not a wall at all.

